# The server package

`danu-server` installs the pipeline the way a package should: entry points in
`/usr/bin`, configuration in `/etc/danu`, data in `/var/lib/danu`, rebuildable
working directories in `/var/cache/danu`, units in `/usr/lib/systemd/system`.

    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

`isofill` is a dependency rather than a bundled copy; it has its own package
built from its own repository. GDAL comes from the distribution for the same
reason it is absent from `pyproject.toml`: the PyPI builds are not worth
relying on.

The editor is not in this package. It is packaged separately, from the same
source, so that what it previews is what this produces.
